SUMMARY:Pioneer Winter Collective
DESCRIPTION:Co-presented by American Dance Festival and The Carolina Theatre • ADF Debut\nProgram: Apollo\nRunning time: 55 minutes\, no intermission\nTickets: $30 plus fees and taxes\nTickets are purchased through The Carolina Theatre’s Box Office. Ticket packages & discounts do not apply. \nCompany Website: pioneerwinter.com \nApollo is a dance-theater work exploring intergenerational queer dynamics\, memory\, HIV/AIDS\, and legacy. This biomythography uses dance-theater to delve into the intersection of personal history\, cultural memory\, and mythology. Apollo centers on legacy and connection and features bodies and voices that are left out of the canon. It confronts ageism and reimagines who gets to be seen and celebrated on stage. The work expands on what dance can be so bodies survive\, thrive\, and are witnessed. \nPhoto Credit: Karli Evans
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/pioneer-winter-collective/
LOCATION:Carolina Theatre of Durham\, 309 W Morgan St\, Durham\, NC\, 27701\, United States
CATEGORIES:Dance,Festival,LGBTQ,Live Performance
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://downtowndurham.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Pioneer-Winter-Collective-Photo-by-Karli-Evans.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Carolina Theatre of Durham":MAILTO:noreply@facebookmail.com
GEO:35.9977171;-78.9029223
